<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.13.1: Different Features of a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01092</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.13.1: Different Features of a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>86115007-196b-4490-b3f8-434df9c68a76</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Examine the following 4 graphs and think about why 1 of the graphs does not belong in the same group as the other 3.</para>
          <para>
            <figure>
              <media alt="A graph with origin O. The graph is a line crossing the vertical axis and slants downward to cross the horizontal axis.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_16_02_01.svg"/>
              </media>
            </figure>
         </para>
          <para>
            <figure>
              <media alt="A graph. ">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_16_02_02.svg"/>
              </media>
            </figure>
         </para>
          <para>
            <figure>
              <media alt="A graph with origin O. The graph is a horizontal line passing through the middle of the vertical axis.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_16_02_03.svg"/>
              </media>
            </figure>
         </para>
          <para>
            <figure>
              <media alt="A graph.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_16_02_04.svg"/>
              </media>
            </figure>
         </para>
        </problem>
        <solution><para>Which graph does not belong? Be prepared to show your reasoning. 
</para><para>Compare your answers:
       Any answer could be correct.
      Graph A doesn’t belong because:
   </para>
    Graph A doesn't belong because:
    
    Graph A doesn't belong because:
    <list><item> It is the only graph that has a positive vertical intercept and a positive horizontal intercept.</item><item>It is the only one that has a constant, negative rate of change.
     </item></list>
    Graph B doesn't belong because:
    
    Graph B doesn't belong because:
    <list><item> It is the only graph that is not a continuous curve and has multiple pieces.
     </item><item>It is the only one that shows both points and lines.
     </item></list>
    Graph C doesn't belong because:
    
    Graph C doesn't belong because:
    <list><item> It is the only graph that has a constant y-value.
     </item></list>
    Graph D doesn't belong because:
    
    Graph D doesn't belong because:
    <list><item>It is the only graph whose y-value increases and decreases multiple times.
     </item><item>It is the only graph that is not a simple line or curve and that has wave-like features.
     </item></list>
  
  </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
